01:12:12.393 --> 01:12:24.856
[SPEAKER_01]: could be challenged or could be even seen as a wrong propaganda. But my personal principles and what I truly believe is a straightforward

01:12:24.876 --> 01:12:37.276
[SPEAKER_01]: formula. And first of all, there is no, in whatever competition system, doesn't matter what the sport is, There is no such system like global

01:12:37.296 --> 01:12:45.278
[SPEAKER_01]: safety umbrella. This thing is illusion. In the organizations with the maximum investment, like Formula One and similar, you can see that they

01:12:45.318 --> 01:12:59.161
[SPEAKER_01]: have small safety devices being introduced, usually after some kind of serious debacle. Usually. So that means that the absolute safety net

01:12:59.241 --> 01:13:09.309
[SPEAKER_01]: around a person practicing something It's illusion. It's not existent. So if you accept this, then the things are getting simpler. In

01:13:09.489 --> 01:13:22.695
[SPEAKER_01]: paragliding comps, this is a very well established idea. And I think it's the only true safety measure. In paragliding comps, and

01:13:22.735 --> 01:13:35.101
[SPEAKER_01]: especially in the World Cup, the only real safety measure is the pilot quality. That's it. This is it. I mean, I can speak about many other

01:13:35.141 --> 01:13:45.408
